      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.01,
          "end": 7.57,
          "en": "Let's continue with editing our meetups for this backend edit meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 11.62,
          "en": "We have this first case here in this if check where we call update meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "Well, and if I want to add a meetup here, then it's probably here where I want to update one and change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.72,
          "end": 24.75,
          "en": "So again, we'll send a fetch request here and the URL is of course the same as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "And now we won't send a post request because Firebase expects post requests when you add data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 30.57,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "Instead here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "I'm not adding data, but I'm overwriting existing data and in Firebase world and on many other rest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 39.74,
          "en": "APIs as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.75,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "We use a put request for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "With that, we overwrite the existing resource at a certain place on our backend with some new data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 52.86,
          "en": "important that existing resource will keep its ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 54.68,
          "end": 58.7,
          "en": "We then have to set some body and also this header here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 58.7,
          "end": 60.05,
          "en": "So just copy that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.26,
          "end": 62.72,
          "en": "Now the body is a bit tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 62.72,
          "end": 64.49,
          "en": "Not super hard, but a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.73,
          "end": 68.84,
          "en": "It should be our meetup data so we can copy that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "Or actually it should be stringified.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 73.95,
          "en": "JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 75.5,
          "en": "So it should be Json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.51,
          "end": 78.99,
          "en": "But then here it will be an object with our copied meetup data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.99,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "And important here is that you leave out the ID, the ID must be removed because the ID is stored in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "Firebase as a key for your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "It's not in the data itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 91.86,
          "en": "Right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "There is no ID key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "Now locally we add such an ID key though, and there we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "But when I send it back to the server I want to remove that ID key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "Now the good thing is the meetup data we're generating here doesn't have an ID key anyways, and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "we can safely just copy all that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 111.57,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "Now in the meetup store where I update the meetup, I do use the ID to identify the meetup, which needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 125.04,
          "en": "to be updated there, but that's okay because here I'm passing the ID as a separate argument and there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 125.04,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "locally I also have is favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 131.35,
          "en": "Now I also have is favorite on Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 131.35,
          "end": 133.06,
          "en": "It is stored here right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 133.15,
          "end": 139.27,
          "en": "But at the moment if you go back to edit meetup, I'm sending this meetup data which lacks the is favorite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.27,
          "end": 140.2,
          "en": "information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 140.23,
          "end": 145.69,
          "en": "We need that as well because if we leave that out we would overwrite the existing data on Firebase with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 145.69,
          "end": 148.99,
          "en": "our new data, which does not have the is favorite information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 148.99,
          "end": 150.97,
          "en": "And of course we don't want to lose that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 151.93,
          "end": 153.61,
          "en": "Now, what can we do here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.94,
          "end": 159.52,
          "en": "Now, we could certainly find out the is favorite status here, for example, by subscribing to our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 159.52,
          "end": 160.51,
          "en": "meetup store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.51,
          "end": 166.36,
          "en": "But we can also use a different Http request, which is also supported by Firebase, and that would",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 166.36,
          "end": 173.57,
          "en": "be patch put is used to overwrite all the data on the server with the new incoming data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 173.59,
          "end": 180.94,
          "en": "Now that is often what you want, but here we want to overwrite all the data which we provide and keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 180.94,
          "end": 181.87,
          "en": "the rest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 181.87,
          "end": 187.24,
          "en": "And for this we can use patch because that will do just that, whatever is included here in our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 187.24,
          "end": 192.37,
          "en": "So all the key value pairs we're sending will overwrite the existing key value pairs in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 192.49,
          "end": 198.67000000000002,
          "en": "But whatever we're not sending like is favorite is simply capped the not deleted so it merges our incoming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 198.67000000000002,
          "end": 200.44,
          "en": "data with the existing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 200.44,
          "end": 202.24,
          "en": "And that sounds better to me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 202.42000000000002,
          "end": 206.65,
          "en": "So we send a patch request here with our meetup data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 206.78,
          "end": 211.57999999999998,
          "en": "Actually, we don't need to spread it here, therefore we can just send it like that if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 211.57999999999998,
          "end": 213.26,
          "en": "That is our object already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 213.29,
          "end": 214.49,
          "en": "So I'm sending that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 214.49,
          "end": 216.59,
          "en": "And then again we get a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 216.59,
          "end": 223.37,
          "en": "So we have then and catch and we get an error here which we can console log and then we get a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 223.37,
          "end": 230.15,
          "en": "And just as before, of course, here, I want to check if the response is okay, whoops with that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 230.59,
          "end": 233.8,
          "en": "Now, we don't really need to extract any data from the response though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 233.8,
          "end": 236.59,
          "en": "If it's okay, we have all the information we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 236.62,
          "end": 241.36,
          "en": "We're not getting back any ID that we would need because the ID is not changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 241.57,
          "end": 247.66,
          "en": "And yeah, there is no other information we could need, so we don't need to return response Json here",
          "zh": ""
